IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-part2-national-employment-service`

-- Tests of regs 58 and 59 (Part II, National Employment Service). Every expected value is written by hand
-- from the text of the Regulations (SOR-96-332.txt lines 994-1007), never copied from the module's output.

§ `Reg 58(a) -- six matters, four levels`

-- (a) names the situation of the labour market, supply and demand, the economic and employment situations of
-- individuals, families and communities, career and learning trends, social and community conditions, and its
-- probable evolution: six matters; and four levels: Canada as a whole, industries, occupations and areas.
#ASSERT count `reg 58(a) the information the national employment service is to collect and analyse` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT elem `er4 career and learning trends` `reg 58(a) the information the national employment service is to collect and analyse`
#ASSERT elem `er4 the probable evolution of the labour market` `reg 58(a) the information the national employment service is to collect and analyse`
#ASSERT count `reg 58(a) the levels at which the national employment service is to collect and analyse it` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT elem `er4 different occupations` `reg 58(a) the levels at which the national employment service is to collect and analyse it`

§ `Reg 58(b) -- who receives the labour market information`

-- (b) names interested public authorities, the employers' and workers' organizations concerned and the general
-- public; it says nothing about anyone else, so the answer for anyone else is NOTHING, not FALSE.
#ASSERT `reg 58(b) the national employment service is to make labour market information available systematically and promptly to` `er4 an interested public authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 58(b) the national employment service is to make labour market information available systematically and promptly to` `er4 an employers' organization concerned` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 58(b) the national employment service is to make labour market information available systematically and promptly to` `er4 a workers' organization concerned` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 58(b) the national employment service is to make labour market information available systematically and promptly to` `er4 a member of the general public` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 58(b) the national employment service is to make labour market information available systematically and promptly to` `er4 someone else` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 58(c) -- help to workers`

-- (c)(i): a worker; no other condition.
#ASSERT `reg 58(c)(i) the national employment service is to make available information on employment opportunities and on careers and occupations in demand to` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 58(c)(i) the national employment service is to make available information on employment opportunities and on careers and occupations in demand to` FALSE

-- (c)(ii): "where appropriate": a worker and the service's judgment that referral is appropriate.
#ASSERT `reg 58(c)(ii) the national employment service is to refer a worker to other sources of labour market information` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 58(c)(ii) the national employment service is to refer a worker to other sources of labour market information` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 58(c)(ii) the national employment service is to refer a worker to other sources of labour market information` FALSE TRUE

-- (iii): workers seeking employment.
#ASSERT `reg 58(c)(iii) the national employment service is to obtain from a worker the information necessary to effect proper referrals` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 58(c)(iii) the national employment service is to obtain from a worker the information necessary to effect proper referrals` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 58(c)(iii) the national employment service is to obtain from a worker the information necessary to effect proper referrals` FALSE TRUE

-- (iv): in accordance with the local strategies AND when necessary: both are needed.
#ASSERT `reg 58(c)(iv) the national employment service is to interview and counsel a worker and help them develop action plans` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 58(c)(iv) the national employment service is to interview and counsel a worker and help them develop action plans` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 58(c)(iv) the national employment service is to interview and counsel a worker and help them develop action plans` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 58(c)(iv) the national employment service is to interview and counsel a worker and help them develop action plans` FALSE TRUE TRUE

-- (v): particular difficulty obtaining or keeping employment.
#ASSERT `reg 58(c)(v) the national employment service is to provide a worker with information on the availability of special assistance` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `reg 58(c)(v) the national employment service is to provide a worker with information on the availability of special assistance` TRUE FALSE

§ `Reg 58(d) -- help to employers`

#ASSERT count `reg 58(d) the help the national employment service is to give an employer to find suitable workers` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT elem `er4 advising on various ways to meet their employment needs` `reg 58(d) the help the national employment service is to give an employer to find suitable workers`

§ `Reg 59 -- at no cost to all workers, insured or not, claiming or not`

-- A worker gets the service free whatever their insurance or claim status: the rule asks about neither.
#ASSERT `reg 59 the national employment service is to be made available at no cost to` `er4 a worker` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 59 the national employment service is to be made available at no cost to` `er4 an employer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 59 the national employment service is to be made available at no cost to` `er4 a workers' organization` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 59 the national employment service is to be made available at no cost to` `er4 an interested public or private organization providing employment assistance services to workers` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 59 the national employment service is to be made available at no cost to` `er4 someone else` EQUALS NOTHING
